    "prompt":  "Analyze only the real people visible in this cart-camera image.\n\nReturn exactly one valid JSON object and no other text:\n{\"people_count\":2,\"people\":[{\"person_id\":1,\"side\":\"left\",\"distance\":\"mid\",\"motion\":\"moving\",\"direction\":\"frontleft\",\"group_id\":1},{\"person_id\":2,\"side\":\"right\",\"distance\":\"mid\",\"motion\":\"standing\",\"direction\":null,\"group_id\":1}]}\n\nAllowed values:\n- side: left | center | right\n- distance: close | mid | far\n- motion: moving | standing\n- direction for moving people: front | left | right | back | frontleft | frontright | backleft | backright\n- direction for standing people: null\n- group_id: a positive integer shared by visibly grouped people, otherwise null\n\nRules:\n1. Count every clearly visible real person once. Ignore reflections, posters, screens, mannequins, and statues. people_count must equal the number of entries in people. Return {\"people_count\":0,\"people\":[]} when no person is visible.\n2. The camera faces the cart\u0027s forward direction. The thin cyan vertical line is an artificial center guide, not an object. Use torso center: left of the central 20% is left, inside the central 20% is center, and right of it is right. Do not mirror the image.\n3. Estimate apparent distance from visible body height and floor contact: close is over 60% of image height or cropped by an image edge; mid is 30-60%; far is under 30%.\n4. Use moving only with visible motion evidence such as a stride, lifted foot, or walking posture. Otherwise use standing. Do not infer motion from the filename, scene, or prompt.\n5. Direction is relative to the cart: front means away from the camera, back means toward the camera, left and right mean across the image, and diagonal values combine those components. Use body and foot orientation. Never assign a direction to a standing person.\n6. Assign the same group_id only when people are visibly walking together, standing together, or interacting. Start group IDs at 1. Nearby people without clear grouping receive null.\n7. Output only the fields shown in the example. Do not output costs, radii, explanations, scene text, or navigation advice.",
